# Walkthrough — Live Screenshot Processing Pipeline Log & Diagnostics Fix

## 1. Summary of Changes & Diagnostic Fix

### Screenshot Detection Scope Fix ([`app.py`](file:///c:/github/textline/app.py))
- **Root Cause Identified**: `monitor_clipboard()` previously generated a new `pipeline_id` and emitted `SCREENSHOT_DETECTED` on every 1-second polling loop *before* checking `if current_hash != last_image_hash:`. As a result, static images on the clipboard produced detached events every second, while new screenshot processing (`status_update: processing`) inside `if current_hash != last_image_hash:` did not emit `SCREENSHOT_DETECTED`.
- **Fix Applied**: Moved `pipeline_id = generate_pipeline_id()` and `emit_pipeline_log(pipeline_id, "SCREENSHOT_DETECTED", ...)` directly **inside** `if current_hash != last_image_hash:`.
- **Guaranteed Execution Path**:
  ```text
  monitor_clipboard()
        ↓
  ImageGrab.grabclipboard() (isinstance Image)
        ↓
  current_hash != last_image_hash  (NEW SCREENSHOT DETECTED!)
        ↓
  pipeline_id = generate_pipeline_id()
        ↓
  emit_pipeline_log(pipeline_id, "SCREENSHOT_DETECTED", "New screenshot detected in clipboard")
        ↓
  emit_pipeline_log(pipeline_id, "CLIPBOARD_READ_SUCCESS", ...)
        ↓
  emit_pipeline_log(pipeline_id, "IMAGE_VALIDATION_SUCCESS", ...)
        ↓
  emit_pipeline_log(pipeline_id, "IMAGE_PREPARATION_START", ...)
        ↓
  socketio.emit('status_update', {'status': 'processing', ...})
        ↓
  generate_content_with_fallback(..., pipeline_id=pipeline_id)
        ↓
  socketio.emit('status_update', {'status': 'success', ...})
        ↓
  emit_pipeline_log(pipeline_id, "PIPELINE_COMPLETE", ...)
  ```

